---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '@components/Breadcrumb.astro';

const title = "Terms of Service";
const description = "MaterialCal terms of service. Use of the site, calculator disclaimers, intellectual property, and limitation of liability.";
const lastUpdated = "November 18, 2026";
---

<BaseLayout title={`${title} | MaterialCal`} description={description}>
  <div class="container content-wrapper">
    <Breadcrumb trail={[
      { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
      { label: 'Terms of Service' }
    ]} />

    <article class="content legal">
      <header class="page-header">
        <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
        <p class="updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
      </header>

      <p>
        These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your use of the MaterialCal website
        ("the Site", "we", "us"). By accessing or using the Site, you agree to be bound by these
        Terms. If you don't agree, please don't use the Site.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Use of the Site</h2>
      <p>
        MaterialCal provides free online calculators for construction, landscaping, and material
        estimation. You may use the Site for personal or commercial purposes without registration,
        subject to these Terms.
      </p>
      <p>You agree NOT to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Use the Site for any illegal purpose or in violation of any laws</li>
        <li>Attempt to gain unauthorized access to the Site, our servers, or other users' data</li>
        <li>Use automated tools (bots, scrapers) to extract data beyond what's permitted by our <code>robots.txt</code></li>
        <li>Interfere with or disrupt the Site, including overloading our servers</li>
        <li>Misrepresent your affiliation with us or any other entity</li>
        <li>Copy, reproduce or republish substantial portions of our content without permission (see Intellectual Property below)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. Calculator Accuracy and Disclaimer</h2>
      <p>
        Our calculators are <strong>estimating tools</strong>, not engineering substitutes. They
        produce theoretical results based on input dimensions and average material density values.
        Actual material orders should account for:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Local supplier variation in density and grading</li>
        <li>Moisture content (wet materials weigh significantly more)</li>
        <li>Compaction and settling during installation</li>
        <li>Project-specific waste and irregularities</li>
        <li>Site conditions, drainage, and grading requirements</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <strong>For any project involving structural integrity, building permits, or significant
        financial commitment, consult a licensed professional engineer, contractor, or architect.</strong>
        Our calculators are not a substitute for professional engineering judgment, code compliance
        review, or supplier-specific quotes.
      </p>
      <p>
        We make reasonable efforts to ensure formulas, density values and pricing references are
        accurate and current. However, we make no guarantee of accuracy and accept no liability
        for decisions made based on calculator results.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Intellectual Property</h2>
      <p>
        All content on the Site — including calculator interfaces, design, text, images, code,
        formulas presentations, reference tables, and FAQs — is the property of MaterialCal or
        our content contributors, protected by copyright and other intellectual property laws.
      </p>
      <p>You may:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Use calculator results for personal and commercial projects</li>
        <li>Reference and quote short excerpts from articles with attribution and a link back to the source page</li>
        <li>Embed our calculators on your own site using our official embed code (when available)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>You may not:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Copy or republish substantial portions of our written content without permission</li>
        <li>Re-host our calculator code or recreate functionality that's substantially similar</li>
        <li>Remove or modify attribution when using embed widgets</li>
        <li>Use our brand name "MaterialCal" or our logos without written consent</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        For permission requests, contact <a href="mailto:contact@materialcal.com">contact@materialcal.com</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Third-Party Links</h2>
      <p>
        The Site may contain links to third-party websites including affiliate links to suppliers
        like Home Depot, Lowe's, and Amazon. These third-party sites are not under our control,
        and we are not responsible for their content, privacy practices, or accuracy.
      </p>
      <p>
        Affiliate links may pay us a small commission if you make a purchase. This does not affect
        the price you pay. Our editorial recommendations are not influenced by affiliate
        relationships — we link to commonly accessible suppliers regardless of commission.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        The Site displays advertising from Google AdSense and may display additional ads from
        select partners. We don't control which specific ads appear; placement is automated.
        If you believe an ad is misleading, illegal, or harmful, please report it to us and we
        will work with the ad network to address it.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Limitation of Liability</h2>
      <p>
        TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW, MATERIALCALC AND ITS OPERATORS SHALL
        NOT BE LIABLE FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES
        ARISING FROM YOUR USE OF THE SITE, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Material under-orders or over-orders based on calculator results</li>
        <li>Project failures attributed to calculator-based estimates</li>
        <li>Lost profits, lost data, or business interruption</li>
        <li>Errors or omissions in calculator formulas, density values, or price references</li>
        <li>Third-party services linked from the Site</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        OUR TOTAL CUMULATIVE LIABILITY FOR ANY CLAIM ARISING FROM OR RELATED TO THE SITE SHALL NOT
        EXCEED $50 USD.
      </p>

      <h2>7. No Warranty</h2>
      <p>
        THE SITE IS PROVIDED "AS IS" AND "AS AVAILABLE" WITHOUT WARRANTIES OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS
        OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A
        PARTICULAR PURPOSE, OR NON-INFRINGEMENT.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Our handling of your information is governed by our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>,
        which is incorporated into these Terms by reference.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Modifications</h2>
      <p>
        We may revise these Terms at any time. Material changes will be flagged on the Site for
        30 days before taking effect. Your continued use of the Site after changes constitutes
        acceptance of the revised Terms. The "Last updated" date reflects the most recent revision.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Termination</h2>
      <p>
        We reserve the right to refuse service, block access, or otherwise restrict use of the
        Site to any user, at our discretion, for any reason — including violation of these Terms.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Governing Law</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms are governed by the laws of the United States and the State of Delaware,
        without regard to conflict-of-law principles. Any disputes arising from these Terms
        shall be resolved in the state or federal courts located in Delaware.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these Terms: <a href="mailto:contact@materialcal.com">contact@materialcal.com</a>
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .content-wrapper { max-width: var(--content-max); }
  .page-header { padding: var(--s-6) 0 var(--s-5); }
  .updated { color: var(--n500); font-size: 14px; margin-top: 8px; }
  .legal p { line-height: 1.7; font-size: 15px; }
  .legal ul { font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.7; }
  .legal ul li { margin-bottom: var(--s-2); }
  .legal h2 { font-size: 20px; }
  .legal h3 { font-size: 16px; margin-top: var(--s-4); }
  .legal code { background: var(--n100); padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 3px; font-size: 13px; }
</style>
